description:
## Overview

Improve the user experience for circuit breaker states in the web portal.

## Context

Circuit breakers protect services from cascading failures by temporarily blocking requests to failing services. The portal should clearly communicate circuit breaker states to users.

## Current State

- Circuit breaker logic may exist in backend
- No clear UX for indicating when services are in circuit-broken state
- Users may not understand why requests are failing

## Requirements

1. **Visual indicators**
   - Banner/toast when service is circuit-broken
   - Countdown timer showing when circuit will retry
   - Historical view of circuit breaker events

2. **User guidance**
   - Explanation of what circuit breaker means
   - Suggested actions (wait, contact support)
   - Link to status page

3. **Recovery indication**
   - Notification when circuit closes
   - Success indicator on recovery

## Implementation

### Circuit Breaker Status Component

```typescript
// src/components/CircuitBreakerBanner.tsx
interface CircuitBreakerBannerProps {
  service: string;
  state: 'closed' | 'open' | 'half-open';
  retryAfter?: Date;
}

export const CircuitBreakerBanner: React.FC<CircuitBreakerBannerProps> = ({
  service,
  state,
  retryAfter,
}) => {
  if (state === 'closed') return null;

  return (
    <Alert variant="warning">
      <AlertTitle>{service} is temporarily unavailable</AlertTitle>
      <AlertDescription>
        {state === 'open' && (
          <>Service is experiencing issues. Retrying in <Countdown to={retryAfter} /></>
        )}
        {state === 'half-open' && (
          <>Testing service availability...</>
        )}
      </AlertDescription>
    </Alert>
  );
};
```

## Files to Create/Modify

- `web/portal/src/components/CircuitBreakerBanner.tsx` (new)
- `web/portal/src/hooks/useCircuitBreakerStatus.ts` (new)
- `web/portal/src/lib/http/client.ts` - Add circuit breaker state handling
- API response handling to detect circuit breaker errors

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Banner displays when service circuit-breaks
- [ ] Countdown timer shows retry time
- [ ] Notification when service recovers
- [ ] Clear explanation for non-technical users
- [ ] Works on mobile devices
- [ ] Unit tests for components

