## Task

When `enabled: false` is set, the operator should scale the workload to zero replicas instead of just updating the status.

**File**: `operators/ai-model-operator/controllers/aimodel_controller.go`

### Current Behavior

```go
if !aimodel.Spec.Enabled {
    aimodel.Status.Phase = "Disabled"
    return ctrl.Result{}, nil  // Does nothing to the workload!
}
```

### Desired Behavior with KServe

With InferenceService, use annotation to scale to zero:

```go
if !aimodel.Spec.Enabled {
    // Scale InferenceService to zero
    isvc := &kservev1beta1.InferenceService{}
    if err := r.Get(ctx, types.NamespacedName{Name: aimodel.Name, Namespace: aimodel.Namespace}, isvc); err == nil {
        // Use KServe annotation to disable
        if isvc.Annotations == nil {
            isvc.Annotations = make(map[string]string)
        }
        isvc.Annotations["autoscaling.knative.dev/min-scale"] = "0"
        isvc.Annotations["autoscaling.knative.dev/max-scale"] = "0"
        if err := r.Update(ctx, isvc); err != nil {
            return ctrl.Result{}, err
        }
    }
    aimodel.Status.Phase = "Disabled"
    return ctrl.Result{}, nil
}
```

Or delete the InferenceService and recreate when re-enabled:

```go
if !aimodel.Spec.Enabled {
    // Delete InferenceService to stop all pods
    isvc := &kservev1beta1.InferenceService{}
    if err := r.Get(ctx, types.NamespacedName{Name: aimodel.Name, Namespace: aimodel.Namespace}, isvc); err == nil {
        if err := r.Delete(ctx, isvc); err != nil {
            return ctrl.Result{}, err
        }
    }
    aimodel.Status.Phase = "Disabled"
    return ctrl.Result{}, nil
}
```

### Re-enabling

When `enabled: true`, the normal reconcile flow recreates the InferenceService.

### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `enabled: false` stops the model serving
- [ ] GPU resources are released when disabled
- [ ] Re-enabling restores service
- [ ] Status shows "Disabled" when disabled

